/bin/zsh -lc "<lab>/.venv/bin/python -c 'from pathlib import Path
import model,numpy as np
original=model.load(\"model_in.json\")
# Interval arithmetic proves that 1024 exceeds every possible positive logit.
lo=np.zeros(20);hi=np.ones(20)
for i,(w,b) in enumerate(original):
 low=lo@np.maximum(w,0)+hi@np.minimum(w,0)+b
 high=hi@np.maximum(w,0)+lo@np.minimum(w,0)+b
 lo,hi=low,high
 if i<len(original)-1:lo=np.maximum(lo,0);hi=np.maximum(hi,0)
assert hi[0]<1024
edited=[]
# Carry users_affected and maintenance_window through the existing hidden layers.
for k,(w,b) in enumerate(original[:-1]):
 nw=np.zeros((w.shape[0]+(2 if k else 0),w.shape[1]+2))
 nw[:w.shape[0],:w.shape[1]]=w
 if k==0:nw[2,-2]=1;nw[9,-1]=1
 else:nw[-2,-2]=1;nw[-1,-1]=1
 edited.append((nw,np.r_[b,0.,0.]))
w,b=original[-1]
# p=ReLU(F), n=ReLU(-F), t=ReLU(u-.5+m-1), m.
nw=np.zeros((w.shape[0]+2,4));nw[:w.shape[0],0]=w[:,0];nw[:w.shape[0],1]=-w[:,0]
nw[-2,2]=1;nw[-1,2]=1;nw[-1,3]=1
edited.append((nw,np.array([b[0],-b[0],-1.5,0.])))
# a=ReLU(p-1024m), t, r=ReLU(t-p), n.
nw=np.array([[1,0,-1,0],[0,0,0,1],[0,1,1,0],[-1024,0,0,0]],float)
edited.append((nw,np.zeros(4)))
edited.append((np.array([[1],[1],[-1],[-1]],float),np.zeros(1)))
model.save(edited,\"model_out.json\")
notes=\"\"\"Inferred earlier rules:
1. Ignore tone_anger.
2. Repair EU under-escalation with the existing +17 EU score offset.
3. Escalate critical-tier alerts when error_rate > 0.70.
4. When confidence < 0.40, urgency > 0.20, and retry_count < 0.99, also escalate if increasing impact by 0.50 (capped at 1) makes the corrected base decision positive.

New rule: suppress alerts when maintenance_window = 1 and users_affected <= 0.50. Otherwise retain the current decision. All eight query answers match candidate A, including suppression at exactly 0.50 and escalation at 0.51.

I retained all existing hidden computations and carried users_affected and maintenance_window to an added ReLU gate. Let p=ReLU(F), n=ReLU(-F), t=ReLU(users_affected-0.50+maintenance_window-1). The output is ReLU(p-1024*maintenance_window)+t-ReLU(t-p)-n. Interval arithmetic bounds F above by 563.886, so 1024 disables the first term during maintenance. Outside maintenance the output equals F. During maintenance it equals min(p,ReLU(users_affected-0.50))-n. Thus only the specified decisions change.

All weights follow algebraic reasoning. No training, fitting, or solver was used.
\"\"\"
Path(\"NOTES.md\").write_text(notes)
print(\"Saved model_out.json and NOTES.md; notes words:\",len(notes.split()),\"output upper bound:\",hi[0])'" in $WSROOT/large/s0/sol-query8w-r2/step5
